BBands wrote:
> Hello,
> 
> Is there any support planned for Python 2.5, either Windows or Linux?

I expect so.

> I gather that this would mean a switch to NumPy.

Not really.

The only trick is installing Numeric on Python 2.5 on Windows as they 
don't provide an installer.  Its one way to encourage people to move to 
NumPy ;)

BioPython is another project still using Numeric, and they built their 
own Numeric Windows installer for Python 2.3, you can download it here:

http://biopython.org/wiki/Download
http://biopython.org/DIST/Numeric-24.2.win32-py2.5.exe

Peter

